meta {
  name: Inline person on update is refused
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "person": {
      "username": "ishaan.verma",
      "first_name": "Ishaan",
      "last_name": "Verma"
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
}

docs {
  400, because the alternative readings are all worse. Creating a second
  identity for a student who already has one would be a duplicate account;
  editing the linked person through the student route would hide a write to a
  different row behind a student PATCH; moving the student onto a new person
  would be an account takeover. So the field is simply not accepted here, and
  you PATCH /persons/{id} instead - request 12.

  The same 400 comes back from PATCH /staff/{id} and PATCH /guardians/{id}.
}
